WEBVTT

00:01:12.220 --> 00:01:13.550
In 1964,

00:01:14.020 --> 00:01:15.890
Akagi has resurfaced after six years

00:01:15.890 --> 00:01:18.320
alongside the police officer Yasuoka.

00:01:18.320 --> 00:01:21.280
However, that Akagi was fake.

00:01:22.070 --> 00:01:25.690
Even though he's fake, 
he still displays amazing skill.

00:01:25.690 --> 00:01:29.250
But he now faces the real Akagi.

00:01:26.830 --> 00:01:30.070
<b>Episode 9</b>

00:01:26.830 --> 00:01:30.070
<b>The Authenticity of Genius</b>

00:01:32.900 --> 00:01:33.570
He got it right!

00:01:34.090 --> 00:01:38.270
He guessed the shanten number 
before the tiles were even revealed!

00:01:39.930 --> 00:01:42.340
This is interesting.

00:01:43.030 --> 00:01:46.010
Boss, this isn't that amazing.

00:01:46.360 --> 00:01:47.450
Meaning?

00:01:47.450 --> 00:01:48.910
It's quite simple.

00:01:48.910 --> 00:01:52.430
So you're saying that this 
wasn't based on instinct,

00:01:52.430 --> 00:01:54.260
but that there was a trick?

00:01:55.130 --> 00:01:57.840
It's nothing that elaborate,

00:01:57.840 --> 00:02:00.630
but anyone could arrive at it 
if they think a bit.

00:02:01.770 --> 00:02:04.400
There are 136 tiles in total.

00:02:04.400 --> 00:02:09.170
Out of those, 13 x 9, or 117 
tiles, are already uncovered.

00:02:09.620 --> 00:02:11.400
Which leaves 19 remaining tiles.

00:02:11.990 --> 00:02:14.690
With enough time, 
figuring out what those 19 tiles are

00:02:14.690 --> 00:02:17.180
is something even a 
grade schooler could do.

00:02:17.650 --> 00:02:21.680
Which means that the remaining 
tiles are the 13 tiles I just opened

00:02:22.500 --> 00:02:26.240
and a 1 and 7 of circles, 
1 and 3 of bamboo,

00:02:26.240 --> 00:02:27.780
and two of the 9 of characters.

00:02:27.780 --> 00:02:29.820
With these 6 tiles, we have 
the remaining 19 tiles.

00:02:31.030 --> 00:02:33.880
Fake Akagi's claim is that 
figuring the shanten number

00:02:33.880 --> 00:02:36.440
isn't difficult to a player of this level.

00:02:37.610 --> 00:02:40.320
Among these 19 tiles, 
there isn't a single set of three.

00:02:40.320 --> 00:02:43.600
Based on that fact alone, 
it couldn't be better than 2 shanten.

00:02:44.540 --> 00:02:47.280
That's because, in Mahjong, 
a hand can only be in

00:02:47.280 --> 00:02:50.110
2 shanten once one set of three 
and the pair are complete.

00:02:50.790 --> 00:02:53.940
These 19 tiles do not 
satisfy that condition.

00:02:53.940 --> 00:02:59.610
No matter how you pick the 13 tiles, 
you'll get 3 sets of two, no matter what.

00:03:00.690 --> 00:03:04.430
Which means the worst you 
could get is 5 shanten.

00:03:04.430 --> 00:03:07.030
But the chance for that is fleetingly low.

00:03:07.690 --> 00:03:11.030
You might get it once in a few hundred tries.

00:03:11.030 --> 00:03:13.530
So it's either a 3 or 4 shanten.

00:03:14.640 --> 00:03:16.030
50:50.

00:03:16.780 --> 00:03:21.790
Actually, judging from the tiles 
here, a 3 shanten is more likely.

00:03:22.530 --> 00:03:25.880
It'll probably be 3 shanten 
six or seven out of ten times.

00:03:26.360 --> 00:03:31.380
So even blurting out 3 shanten without 
thinking has a 65% chance of being correct.

00:03:31.820 --> 00:03:34.010
It's simple probability.

00:03:34.010 --> 00:03:35.890
Not instinct at all!

00:03:36.740 --> 00:03:39.890
You might be able to deceive people 
not familiar with probability,

00:03:39.890 --> 00:03:42.630
but that won't work on me, Akagi-san.

00:03:47.070 --> 00:03:49.030
I see, you are second-rate.

00:03:49.430 --> 00:03:50.330
What did you say?!

00:03:51.100 --> 00:03:52.820
You're way off.

00:03:53.280 --> 00:03:54.970
So you're trying to tell me

00:03:54.970 --> 00:03:57.280
you got this not through 
probability, but through instinct?

00:03:57.280 --> 00:03:58.340
Who knows?

00:03:59.650 --> 00:04:01.340
Then prove it.

00:04:06.400 --> 00:04:11.050
Add three tiles to these ten here 
and make it a 4 shanten hand.

00:04:11.820 --> 00:04:15.360
But you have to pick 
from these nine tiles.

00:04:20.820 --> 00:04:22.630
Pick three tiles from here.

00:04:23.580 --> 00:04:27.140
If you can actually make a 4 shanten 
hand with this, I'll believe...

00:04:27.890 --> 00:04:31.140
that you have an instinct 
that surpasses probability.

00:04:35.650 --> 00:04:36.890
<i>That's impossible.</i>

00:04:36.890 --> 00:04:38.580
<i>There are already 4 sets of two.</i>

00:04:39.070 --> 00:04:41.020
<i>It's already a 4 shanten hand.</i>

00:04:41.020 --> 00:04:43.090
<i>He can't add any more sets of two.</i>

00:04:45.560 --> 00:04:47.270
<i>So of those nine tiles,</i>

00:04:47.270 --> 00:04:50.500
<i>the only tiles he can pick that 
don't break that requirement are...</i>

00:04:50.500 --> 00:04:52.070
<i>These four tiles!</i>

00:04:52.070 --> 00:04:55.670
<i>But drawing two of the 1 of bamboo 
will result in a new set of two,</i>

00:04:55.670 --> 00:04:57.100
<i>so he can only draw one!</i>

00:04:57.980 --> 00:04:59.830
The chances aren't good.

00:05:00.920 --> 00:05:04.410
At first, it might seem that 
the chances aren't so bad,

00:05:04.410 --> 00:05:07.190
seeing that you can 
pick four tiles out of nine.

00:05:07.190 --> 00:05:11.580
However, the chance of actually 
picking these three tiles is under 3%.

00:05:12.330 --> 00:05:14.580
The margin of error is paper thin.

00:05:15.540 --> 00:05:17.310
So, what will you do?

00:05:17.310 --> 00:05:21.460
You'll have to walk a tightrope 
over a pit of defeat.

00:05:22.110 --> 00:05:23.690
Sounds interesting.

00:05:29.610 --> 00:05:31.970
I'll walk that tightrope.

00:05:33.290 --> 00:05:35.580
<i>He's accepting this ridiculous gamble?!</i>

00:05:35.580 --> 00:05:40.640
But you're the one who so 
confidently proposed this challenge.

00:05:41.030 --> 00:05:44.020
I won't hear any complaints about the wager.

00:05:46.180 --> 00:05:47.650
One arm.

00:05:51.540 --> 00:05:52.370
That's ridiculous.

00:05:52.370 --> 00:05:54.550
There's no way I would 
accept that condition!

00:05:56.090 --> 00:05:56.760
Why not?

00:05:57.730 --> 00:05:59.970
Because it's not necessary!

00:05:59.970 --> 00:06:01.980
So you're saying you're not confident?

00:06:01.980 --> 00:06:03.000
I am confident!

00:06:03.750 --> 00:06:06.370
But no matter how low the 
chance is, it's not 0%.

00:06:07.150 --> 00:06:10.270
Even if the chance is as low as 1%,

00:06:10.270 --> 00:06:12.370
there's no way that you 
could wager something

00:06:12.370 --> 00:06:14.110
as irreplaceable as an arm!

00:06:14.630 --> 00:06:16.170
Don't get me wrong.

00:06:16.170 --> 00:06:17.870
I'm not saying that I'm afraid.

00:06:17.870 --> 00:06:20.110
I'm saying that this gamble is idiotic!

00:06:21.010 --> 00:06:24.460
I won't put my life on the line 
for some amusement or game.

00:06:24.460 --> 00:06:26.260
I'm not afraid of dying.

00:06:26.260 --> 00:06:28.680
I just don't want a meaningless death!

00:06:29.280 --> 00:06:30.590
A meaningless death?

00:06:31.640 --> 00:06:34.280
Isn't that precisely what gambling is?

00:06:34.280 --> 00:06:36.440
This "meaningless death," as you call it?

00:06:38.460 --> 00:06:40.930
That's what I've thought all this time.

00:06:41.870 --> 00:06:44.210
We're different types.

00:06:44.210 --> 00:06:47.040
It's not about our types, 
it's about the stage we stand on.

00:06:48.560 --> 00:06:51.600
You've not yet stepped up 
onto the gambling stage.

00:06:52.090 --> 00:06:55.550
That's why you're trying to measure 
gambling with the numbers

00:06:55.550 --> 00:06:57.550
you've squeezed out of your brain.

00:06:58.170 --> 00:07:00.050
Talk about clueless.

00:07:00.050 --> 00:07:00.790
What?

00:07:02.060 --> 00:07:05.170
It's like claiming to know the ocean...

00:07:05.170 --> 00:07:07.790
when you've only gone in waist-deep.

00:07:11.290 --> 00:07:12.680
I see what you're doing.

00:07:13.170 --> 00:07:16.680
You never had the intention 
of accepting this challenge.

00:07:17.020 --> 00:07:19.730
But simply declining would 
make you look incompetent.

00:07:19.730 --> 00:07:23.500
In order to avoid that, 
you claimed to accept the challenge,

00:07:23.500 --> 00:07:25.860
then countered with a 
completely ridiculous wager.

00:07:26.620 --> 00:07:28.420
Your opponent has no 
choice but to back down.

00:07:28.420 --> 00:07:29.890
After that, it was your plan

00:07:29.890 --> 00:07:32.780
to use some abstract arguments 
to confuse everyone.

00:07:32.780 --> 00:07:33.850
Am I wrong?!

00:07:33.850 --> 00:07:35.590
Now, wait.

00:07:36.890 --> 00:07:41.590
Akagi, I do understand what you're saying.

00:07:41.900 --> 00:07:45.440
But we live in different times now.

00:07:46.510 --> 00:07:48.440
You should know that, too.

00:07:51.470 --> 00:07:52.160
Here.

00:07:53.660 --> 00:07:57.030
In this day and age, 
everything is measured with money.

00:07:57.030 --> 00:08:00.580
With the fluidity of money, 
always winning isn't a necessity

00:08:00.580 --> 00:08:03.050
as long as the net result is positive.

00:08:03.400 --> 00:08:08.050
That's why I hold this man and 
his statistics in high regard.

00:08:09.450 --> 00:08:10.750
That's two million there.

00:08:12.630 --> 00:08:15.090
That looks like a salary envelope.

00:08:16.020 --> 00:08:17.130
How about it?

00:08:17.130 --> 00:08:21.340
Why don't you wager your 
salary against my money?

00:08:21.340 --> 00:08:25.030
The difference in amount simply 
reflects the different odds.

00:08:25.030 --> 00:08:26.900
It's like betting on horses.

00:08:30.490 --> 00:08:32.570
I'll bet on a horse, then.

00:08:34.120 --> 00:08:35.780
You shouldn't have done that.

00:08:37.950 --> 00:08:39.830
That man is different.

00:08:40.280 --> 00:08:41.270
Different?

00:08:51.860 --> 00:08:53.770
What are you staring at?

00:08:54.430 --> 00:08:56.300
Do you think you can see through 
the tiles or something?

00:08:56.890 --> 00:08:57.660
Yes.

00:08:59.510 --> 00:09:01.500
If I didn't have that degree of intuition,

00:09:01.910 --> 00:09:06.410
I wouldn't have been able to 
survive these last six years.

00:09:37.760 --> 00:09:39.040
He did it!

00:09:41.500 --> 00:09:44.140
No way... He got those exact three tiles!

00:09:48.670 --> 00:09:50.670
Well, see you later, Boss.

00:09:51.970 --> 00:09:52.550
Hold it!

00:09:55.150 --> 00:09:57.320
I almost missed it.

00:09:57.320 --> 00:10:01.590
The tiles over here... 
Their order has changed slightly.

00:10:02.100 --> 00:10:03.150
If we check,

00:10:03.150 --> 00:10:04.470
a 1 of bamboo, a 4 of bamboo,

00:10:04.470 --> 00:10:05.900
and a 1 of characters should be missing!

00:10:06.230 --> 00:10:09.170
You took them from there!

00:10:09.520 --> 00:10:12.400
The tiles you actually picked 
are still in your hand!

00:10:13.520 --> 00:10:15.970
Oh, you noticed?

00:10:18.120 --> 00:10:23.280
It's a primitive trick, but it's 
pretty effective in practice.

00:10:23.920 --> 00:10:28.170
At the very least, more so than 
your lame probability calculations.

00:10:28.170 --> 00:10:29.120
Shut up.

00:10:29.740 --> 00:10:30.850
Leave the money here.

00:10:31.290 --> 00:10:32.840
Akagi...

00:10:33.930 --> 00:10:36.310
Don't worry, Nangou-san.

00:10:38.860 --> 00:10:40.060
See ya.

00:10:40.570 --> 00:10:41.410
Hey!

00:10:41.840 --> 00:10:42.680
He has them!

00:10:42.680 --> 00:10:43.370
What?

00:10:46.930 --> 00:10:50.370
Even if he hadn't switched 
them out, he still had them!

00:10:50.710 --> 00:10:52.330
The same three tiles!

00:10:52.330 --> 00:10:54.040
No way...

00:10:55.270 --> 00:10:57.830
Checking the remaining tiles 
should give us the proof!

00:11:00.890 --> 00:11:04.000
They're not there... 
those three tiles...

00:11:04.730 --> 00:11:07.310
Don't get involved with that man.

00:11:10.530 --> 00:11:12.530
Leave him alone.

00:11:17.780 --> 00:11:19.470
Oh, that's it, Osamu.

00:11:21.070 --> 00:11:24.150
Mentanpin, iipeikou, two dora.

00:11:24.150 --> 00:11:25.260
What?

00:11:25.770 --> 00:11:27.910
Aw man, I was just in first place.

00:11:27.910 --> 00:11:29.860
What a shame.

00:11:30.650 --> 00:11:32.580
Yeah, real shame.

00:11:34.420 --> 00:11:36.080
You're back late.

00:11:37.820 --> 00:11:39.750
If you'd come home a bit earlier,

00:11:39.750 --> 00:11:41.850
you could have joined the fun.

00:11:41.850 --> 00:11:43.320
Right, Kawashima?

00:11:43.320 --> 00:11:45.860
Yeah, but unfortunately...

00:11:46.500 --> 00:11:48.360
we're on our last East-South match.

00:11:49.580 --> 00:11:50.390
How's it going?

00:11:50.390 --> 00:11:51.860
Not good.

00:11:51.860 --> 00:11:54.450
They took most of my pay.

00:12:01.320 --> 00:12:04.880
<i>Osamu and Kawashima have both been losing.</i>

00:12:06.380 --> 00:12:07.870
<i>I see.</i>

00:12:07.870 --> 00:12:09.120
This is a setup.

00:12:10.190 --> 00:12:11.490
If all three were to win,

00:12:11.490 --> 00:12:14.450
the impression that they're 
scalping Osamu would be too obvious.

00:12:15.050 --> 00:12:18.560
To avoid this, they pick 
a loser before starting.

00:12:19.480 --> 00:12:24.870
Afterwards, only the money Osamu 
lost will be split between those three.

00:12:28.080 --> 00:12:29.800
I hate losing this much.

00:12:30.380 --> 00:12:33.070
It's getting to be too stupid to keep up.

00:12:33.410 --> 00:12:35.170
Chill, man. Don't be so down.

00:12:35.170 --> 00:12:36.810
Fortitude can still pay off.

00:12:36.980 --> 00:12:37.880
Whatever.

00:12:38.240 --> 00:12:38.940
Pon!

00:12:40.260 --> 00:12:42.910
How can you have all those?

00:12:42.910 --> 00:12:45.020
Osamu, be careful. 
You're in second place.

00:12:45.400 --> 00:12:46.310
Yeah...

00:12:48.020 --> 00:12:50.520
Dealing into a big one will be bad.

00:12:50.520 --> 00:12:53.260
Bah, nothing to deal into, anyway.

00:12:53.260 --> 00:12:54.260
Figures I'd get a trash hand.

00:12:55.260 --> 00:12:59.770
I don't trust what you call a "trash hand."

00:13:01.340 --> 00:13:03.540
That's it! Sorry, Kawashima.

00:13:05.650 --> 00:13:08.510
South, toitoi, so 5,200.

00:13:05.650 --> 00:13:08.510
Toitoi - A hand consisting of all triplets or quads, and a pair.

00:13:08.510 --> 00:13:11.040
Ah, screw this!

00:13:11.720 --> 00:13:13.630
<i>So, they're signaling each other.</i>

00:13:15.470 --> 00:13:21.690
These three were signaling each other 
with the first words of their sentences.

00:13:21.690 --> 00:13:23.380
<i>Chill, man. Don't be so down.</i>

00:13:23.380 --> 00:13:25.490
<i>Fortitude can still pay off.</i>

00:13:25.490 --> 00:13:27.520
The "ch" of "chill" signifies character tiles.

00:13:27.520 --> 00:13:29.870
The "for" of "fortitude" 
signifies the number four.

00:13:29.870 --> 00:13:33.230
So that was a signal to 
discard the 4 of characters.

00:13:33.230 --> 00:13:34.530
Similarly...

00:13:34.530 --> 00:13:37.180
<i>Bah, nothing to deal into, anyway.</i>

00:13:37.180 --> 00:13:38.100
<i>Figures I'd get a trash hand.</i>

00:13:38.790 --> 00:13:41.750
That was a signal to discard 
the <i>fi</i>ve of <i>ba</i>mboo.

00:13:43.190 --> 00:13:45.800
<i>No wonder he's getting hustled,</i>

00:13:45.800 --> 00:13:48.010
<i>if he can't even figure out this simple trick.</i>

00:13:49.800 --> 00:13:50.810
Damn it.

00:13:52.350 --> 00:13:55.890
Kawashima and his gang keep winning 
quick hands even in South Hand 3.

00:13:58.140 --> 00:14:00.520
And at the beginning of South Hand 4...

00:14:03.780 --> 00:14:06.860
While everybody is still 
focusing on their own tiles...

00:14:09.630 --> 00:14:11.600
Kawashima cheats.

00:14:12.500 --> 00:14:15.600
He deposits tiles he doesn't 
need on the left end of the wall

00:14:17.780 --> 00:14:20.840
and retrieves good tiles he had 
placed at the right end of the wall.

00:14:21.510 --> 00:14:24.130
This cheat is known as uprooting.

00:14:25.410 --> 00:14:27.670
A simple, straightforward cheat.

00:14:28.110 --> 00:14:31.680
But since your hand shrinks 
for just one moment,

00:14:31.680 --> 00:14:33.950
being spotted means it's over.

00:14:35.230 --> 00:14:37.360
<i>That dimwit didn't notice anything.</i>

00:14:40.090 --> 00:14:41.400
<i>What's that look?</i>

00:14:41.400 --> 00:14:42.600
<i>Did he notice?</i>

00:14:46.890 --> 00:14:48.330
<i>Must have imagined that.</i>

00:14:51.620 --> 00:14:54.110
I'll be taking this, then.

00:14:55.500 --> 00:14:58.110
Sorry. If I had played...

00:14:58.860 --> 00:15:02.350
No, I'm the one who blew it.

00:15:05.810 --> 00:15:06.900
You guys...

00:15:09.270 --> 00:15:11.360
How about a little game with me?

00:15:12.020 --> 00:15:14.600
Tomorrow. We're tired.

00:15:18.980 --> 00:15:20.830
Still tired?

00:15:21.620 --> 00:15:22.770
Where did you get that?!

00:15:23.340 --> 00:15:25.210
It's easy money.

00:15:25.210 --> 00:15:28.770
If you beat me in this little 
gamble, it's yours to take.

00:15:30.850 --> 00:15:32.280
What is this game going to be?

00:15:35.710 --> 00:15:39.120
Osamu's hand was in tenpai with a 
closed wait for a the 5 of characters.

00:15:39.830 --> 00:15:42.960
If I can't complete it by 
drawing twice from the 14 tiles

00:15:44.040 --> 00:15:46.450
in the dead wall, you win.

00:15:50.330 --> 00:15:52.970
If I do complete it, I win.

00:15:54.080 --> 00:15:55.340
In that event,

00:15:55.340 --> 00:15:59.710
I'll take your winnings for today, 
this month's pay, and your savings.

00:16:00.410 --> 00:16:02.860
Meaning your bank books 
and signature seals.

00:16:02.860 --> 00:16:04.530
Wh-What?

00:16:05.070 --> 00:16:09.440
Normally, nobody would accept this 
reckless gamble for their life savings.

00:16:09.880 --> 00:16:10.720
However...

00:16:11.290 --> 00:16:13.620
Sounds fun. We'll accept!

00:16:13.620 --> 00:16:15.350
H-Hey!

00:16:17.690 --> 00:16:19.510
What the hell are you thinking?

00:16:20.810 --> 00:16:22.360
Look at the table.

00:16:23.750 --> 00:16:25.880
The tile Osamu is waiting 
for, the 5 of characters.

00:16:26.620 --> 00:16:28.100
One's the dora indicator.

00:16:28.610 --> 00:16:30.600
Another in Furuya's discards.

00:16:30.600 --> 00:16:33.590
Where do you think the other two are?

00:16:34.820 --> 00:16:37.750
They're face down in my hand.

00:16:39.390 --> 00:16:41.860
That means it's empty?

00:16:41.860 --> 00:16:43.930
That's right.

00:16:43.930 --> 00:16:48.160
He won't get it, no matter if 
he draws twice or ten times.

00:16:50.070 --> 00:16:52.020
That's all of our money.

00:16:52.880 --> 00:16:54.120
Very well.

00:16:56.510 --> 00:16:57.970
Then, here I go.

00:17:00.260 --> 00:17:01.780
You moron!

00:17:01.780 --> 00:17:03.600
You can't pick the dora indicator!

00:17:04.990 --> 00:17:06.280
I can't?

00:17:06.280 --> 00:17:10.240
You can't think you can win 
by picking a tile that's face-up!

00:17:11.030 --> 00:17:12.610
That was just a joke.

00:17:21.150 --> 00:17:22.380
He changed his hand?!

00:17:22.380 --> 00:17:23.890
Wait!

00:17:23.890 --> 00:17:25.860
Who said that you could 
change your hand?!

00:17:26.330 --> 00:17:30.610
Two draws naturally includes 
changing the hand.

00:17:30.610 --> 00:17:31.860
I can't compromise that rule.

00:17:33.050 --> 00:17:37.200
I bet you have the last two 
5 of characters tiles, anyway.

00:17:38.590 --> 00:17:41.240
How shamelessly greedy of you 
to try to win big money

00:17:41.760 --> 00:17:42.940
with zero risk.

00:17:46.890 --> 00:17:49.630
<i>It's a double pon wait for a 
west wind or 6 of characters.</i>

00:17:49.630 --> 00:17:53.450
<i>I think there's still one west 
wind left in the dead wall.</i>

00:17:53.450 --> 00:17:56.070
<i>It's a 1:12 chance.</i>

00:17:56.070 --> 00:17:57.320
<i>There's no way he'll get it.</i>

00:17:58.450 --> 00:18:01.690
All right, we'll accept that.

00:18:01.690 --> 00:18:02.760
Go ahead and draw.

00:18:05.500 --> 00:18:07.160
<i>There's no way he'll get it.</i>

00:18:07.160 --> 00:18:08.660
<i>1:12 chance for that west wind.</i>

00:18:12.210 --> 00:18:15.170
<i>That's the tile I switched out!</i>

00:18:15.170 --> 00:18:19.670
<i>He did notice that I cheated!</i>

00:18:23.070 --> 00:18:24.050
I win.

00:18:26.360 --> 00:18:27.850
I'll just take these.

00:18:32.820 --> 00:18:34.150
What do we do now?

00:18:38.740 --> 00:18:40.550
Is this my salary?

00:18:40.550 --> 00:18:42.340
It's your share.

00:18:42.340 --> 00:18:44.700
I won using your hand.

00:18:45.360 --> 00:18:46.730
Call it a rental fee.

00:18:46.730 --> 00:18:47.430
See ya.

00:18:47.920 --> 00:18:49.190
Where are you going?

00:18:49.190 --> 00:18:50.550
I'm quitting this job.

00:18:50.550 --> 00:18:51.400
What?

00:18:51.400 --> 00:18:53.110
Wait a minute!

00:18:58.180 --> 00:19:02.420
Did you draw the 6 of characters and the 
west wind by chance during that bet?

00:19:03.450 --> 00:19:06.350
There's no way anyone could 
get those by chance.

00:19:06.350 --> 00:19:10.420
I had picked up and switched 
out the 6 of characters.

00:19:11.520 --> 00:19:12.930
I had no idea...

00:19:13.940 --> 00:19:16.440
Remember when I picked 
up the 5 of characters?

00:19:16.440 --> 00:19:17.430
Yes.

00:19:17.740 --> 00:19:20.410
When Kawashima complained 
and told me to put it back,

00:19:20.410 --> 00:19:24.710
I picked up the 6 from the discards 
and switched it with dead wall tile.

00:19:28.910 --> 00:19:31.010
Humans are strange.

00:19:31.010 --> 00:19:33.530
They're alert when you're drawing a tile,

00:19:34.010 --> 00:19:37.160
but let their guard down 
when you return the tile.

00:19:38.170 --> 00:19:41.240
Even more so while they're focusing on the 5.

00:19:41.240 --> 00:19:43.170
They would never realize that

00:19:43.170 --> 00:19:46.480
the seemingly unrelated 6 was replaced

00:19:46.480 --> 00:19:48.160
with something else in the discards.

00:19:48.900 --> 00:19:50.160
It's a psychological blind spot.

00:19:50.560 --> 00:19:52.950
You're right, I didn't notice.

00:19:53.730 --> 00:19:55.800
But what about the west wind?

00:19:55.800 --> 00:19:59.540
You picked that from 
Kawashima-senpai's wall.

00:20:00.090 --> 00:20:02.540
You never touched that wall.

00:20:03.920 --> 00:20:07.050
I didn't need to switch for the west wind.

00:20:07.920 --> 00:20:11.550
He was uprooting tiles 
almost every hand last night.

00:20:12.460 --> 00:20:13.480
Uprooting?

00:20:13.870 --> 00:20:17.290
It's a cheat that replaces 
unwanted tiles with good tiles.

00:20:17.850 --> 00:20:19.930
By counting the honor tiles in his discards,

00:20:19.930 --> 00:20:24.490
it was obvious that the tiles he switched 
out were the east or west wind.

00:20:24.870 --> 00:20:30.310
The challenge was figuring out 
which of those tiles was the west.

00:20:30.310 --> 00:20:32.640
But if you think about it, 
that was easy, too.

00:20:32.640 --> 00:20:34.040
Easy?

00:20:34.040 --> 00:20:36.120
Whenever he used this cheat,

00:20:36.120 --> 00:20:39.500
he had the habit of putting the 
most useless tile to the very left.

00:20:39.910 --> 00:20:42.240
That time, Kawashima was the dealer.

00:20:43.160 --> 00:20:46.700
Meaning that the most useless tile 
could not have been an east wind.

00:20:46.700 --> 00:20:49.720
Isn't that right, Kawashima-senpai?

00:20:53.710 --> 00:20:56.490
Don't think you'll get 
away with this unscathed.

00:20:58.080 --> 00:21:01.500
The genius who descended into 
darkness, Akagi Shigeru.

00:21:02.140 --> 00:21:05.950
Destiny was about to be 
set in motion again,

00:21:05.950 --> 00:21:08.150
accompanied by large waves.

00:22:16.270 --> 00:22:19.230
Next time, "The Announcement 
of the Counterattack."

00:22:17.050 --> 00:22:20.550
<b>Next Episode</b>

00:22:17.050 --> 00:22:20.550
<b>The Announcement of 
the Counterattack</b>
